# class: clearances
# origin: product-roadmap design/rm9.0-coverage-classes.md CV08 (plan-soundness PS2.32: a sofa anchored to a wall, its front on the wall; reduced)
# expect: W_SEAT_FACING_WALL
# status: done
# fact: the loveseat in r_living is turned `rotate 180`, so its front (north) is on the south face of the
#   partition p (y = 2050) with no floor between: nobody can sit on it. A sofa is not `directional`, so
#   nothing turns it for the author.
plan "Living room with a loveseat facing the partition" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 200 { (0,0) (5000,0) (5000,6000) (0,6000) close }
  wall id=p partition thickness 100 { (0,2000) (5000,2000) }
  room id=r_hall at (0,0) size 5000x2000 label "Hall" uses hall
  room id=r_living at (0,2000) size 5000x4000 label "Living" uses living
  door id=d_entry at (2500,0) width 900 wall shell
  door id=d_living at (4200,2000) width 800 wall p swing into r_living
  window at (2500,6000) width 1500 wall shell
  furniture loveseat at (1000,2050) size 1500x850 rotate 180 label "Loveseat" in r_living
}
